        {
          "sourceDoi": "10.1073/pnas.2308668121",
          "targetDoi": "10.1016/j.cpc.2020.107624",
          "snippet": "In recent years, machine learning has emerged as a powerful tool in the study of static and dynamic statistical properties of molecular systems (  18      –  23  ), enabling ab initio simulations of unprecedented scale (  25  ,  26  ). Today, massive amounts of data can be generated by all-atom molecular dynamics (MD) trajectories with ab initio accuracy.",
          "type": "mentioning"
